---
.title = "Temporary files and atomic writes",
.date = "2024-01-01",
.author = "ZigCC",
.layout = "section.shtml",
---

With an ordinary file, truncating and rewriting the destination can expose
partially-written contents to readers, and a crash can leave the destination
incomplete. `std.Io.File.Atomic` writes the new contents to a temporary file
first, then replaces the destination with a rename, so readers see either the
old complete file or the new complete file. This is useful for configuration
files, generated data, and other files that must remain self-consistent.

